# ThreadSanitizer suppression file for craft_client.
# Known false positives. Format: race:<function substring>

# sisl NamedCounter registration race (benign).
#
# craft::read_route_map holds one sisl::StreamTracker per replica, and each StreamTracker carries a
# StreamTrackerMetrics whose constructor calls NamedCounter<name>::set_index() to record the counter's slot.
# NamedCounter<name> is a GLOBAL Meyers singleton shared by every StreamTracker with the same counter name, so
# building a second replica's route map (set_index, a write) races with an in-flight read updating an existing
# one (get_index in StreamTracker::do_update). set_index writes the same index every registration (it is
# idempotent) and get_index reads a plain uint64_t, so the value is always correct -- TSAN flags the
# unsynchronized global, but there is no real hazard. This is a sisl-internal metrics characteristic, not a
# craft_client bug (see the same race noted across the SDS stack).
race:sisl::NamedCounter
